WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.440
Fear is serious business.

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.760
So, it makes sense that anyone with serious
screaming skills might turn out to be pretty

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:10.460
good at showcasing enough of a range of emotions
to become a "somebody" in Hollywood.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:13.780
Here are a few scream queens who became A-listers.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.730
Charlize Theron

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:20.390
For her role as real-life serial killer Aileen
Wuornos in 2003's Monster, actress Charlize

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:21.789
Theron won an Oscar.

00:00:21.789 --> 00:00:25.650
Her loyalty to hair-raising Hollywood pictures
is perhaps due in part to the fact that she

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:31.099
got her start in the horror genre with a small
role in 1995's Children of the Corn III: Urban

00:00:31.099 --> 00:00:32.759
Harvest.

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:33.759
Jennifer Aniston

00:00:33.759 --> 00:00:38.840
Long before Jennifer Aniston became America's
Sweetheart as Rachel Green in Friends, she

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:44.000
made her feature film debut in the 1993 comedy-slasher
flick Leprechaun.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.220
She plays a teen who has to survive a maniacal
leprechaun, hell-bent on recovering his stolen

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:50.220
treasure.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.829
Once Aniston established herself as a rom-com
regular, though, she mostly steered clear

00:00:53.829 --> 00:00:55.730
of any bone-chillers.

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:56.730
Sarah Michelle Gellar

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:02.090
She’s probably best known for her starring
role in the Buffy the Vampire Slayer TV series,

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:05.969
but Sarah Michelle Gellar easily parlayed
her role as a monster-fighting TV heroine

00:01:05.969 --> 00:01:07.490
onto the big screen.

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:11.929
As her career started taking off in 1997,
Gellar starred a pair of slashers, playing

00:01:11.929 --> 00:01:16.310
doomed beauty pageant winner Helen Shivers
in I Know What You Did Last Summer and sorority

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:18.090
sister Cici in Scream 2.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:21.540
"Do you wanna die tonight Cici?"

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.219
Sharon Stone

00:01:23.219 --> 00:01:27.880
Throughout her career, Sharon Stone has proven
she has a basic instinct for selecting solid

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:29.100
starring roles.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:32.299
But before she was a star, she was just another
struggling actress.

00:01:32.299 --> 00:01:37.720
Take, for example, her theatrical debut in
1981's Deadly Blessing, a Wes Craven production

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:41.060
that might've seemed like a sure thing, given
that the director had already established

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:43.759
himself with some solid horror movie credits.

00:01:43.759 --> 00:01:48.469
The pic was both panned and ignored by audiences,
but it did nothing to stop the eventual Oscar

00:01:48.469 --> 00:01:52.209
nominee from ascending to a higher profile
a few years later.

00:01:52.209 --> 00:01:54.119
Mila Kunis

00:01:54.119 --> 00:01:58.849
Her most celebrated role to date came as the
unsettling ballerina Lily in the eerie 2010

00:01:58.849 --> 00:02:04.020
thriller Black Swan, but Mila Kunis’ first
true terror role came courtesy of the 1995

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:05.439
remake of Piranha.

00:02:05.439 --> 00:02:08.920
It wasn't the last time she'd try her hand
at thrillers, and it may not have been the

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:14.620
worst; she also appeared in the critically-eviscerated
American Psycho II: All American Girl, and

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:18.310
the 2007 straight-to-DVD dud Boot Camp.

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:19.850
Renee Zellweger

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:25.100
She might've had everyone at "hello" in her
breakthrough role in the 1996 hit Jerry Maguire.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:29.010
But before Renee Zellweger started tugging
on heart strings in rom-coms like Bridget

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:32.400
Jones' Diary, she did a stint in the horror
house.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:37.580
Her role in Texas Chainsaw Massacre: The Next
Generation was filmed long before she shot

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:41.720
to recognition, but released shortly after
her career started to flourish.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.540
"Aaaahhh!!"

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:45.980
Yikes.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.890
Drew Barrymore

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:52.750
After her memorable role in Steven Spielberg's
E.T.: The Extra Terrestrial, tiny scene-stealer

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:57.420
Drew Barrymore followed her breakout success
with back-to-back Stephen King adaptations:

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:02.430
1984's Firestarter and 1985's Cat's Eye.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:05.990
Barrymore's career cooled later in the '80s,
but she returned to the thriller and horror

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:10.730
genres while building a comeback, starring
in the early '90s efforts Poison Ivy, No Place

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:12.330
to Hide, and Doppelgänger.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:17.600
Her opening cameo in Wes Craven's Scream offered
an obvious nod to her significant scream queen

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:19.250
credentials.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:21.310
Jamie Lee Curtis

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:25.680
Like her mother, Psycho star Janet Leigh,
Jamie Lee Curtis is probably best known for

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.210
her considerable horror movie roots.

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:32.450
In fact, Curtis’ first silver screen appearance
is pretty much what launched her career.

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:37.510
In 1978, she starred as Michael Myers' tortured
sister in John Carpenter's Halloween, the

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:41.650
first of four times she'd appear in the role
over the course of the franchise until 2002.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:47.570
Most recently, she appeared in Fox's cheeky
small-screen slasher satire Scream Queens

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:51.990
as a bit of an homage to her own status as
a lady legend in the field.

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:56.430
Outside of the genre, Curtis has also garnered
plenty of recognition—she's a Golden Globe

00:03:56.430 --> 00:04:00.660
and BAFTA-winning actress—but in spite of
her many subsequent accomplishments, she'll

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:04.050
always probably be known for the closet scene
in Halloween.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.880
Really, how do you ever top that?

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:08.220
Demi Moore

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:12.180
Just before Demi Moore became a member of
the '80s hit-making squad known as "The Brat

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:18.930
Pack," she appeared in a little-known, critically-despised
1982 sci-fi horror flick called Parasite.

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:21.730
"It must kill to survive.

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:24.890
They will unleash the ultimate predator."

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:25.880
"Aahh!"

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:28.040
It wasn't her only stint with the otherworldly.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:33.710
She also starred in the 1988 apocalyptic thriller
The Seventh Sign and the 1990 supernatural

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:38.750
romantic drama Ghost—and she went on to
accrue her fair share of acclaim in non-genre

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:39.750
efforts.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:45.040
Obviously, despite initially unfavorable reviews,
her turn in Parasite didn't gnaw away at her

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:46.040
career prospects.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:47.500
Thanks for watching!

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:51.570
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:54.280
And leave us a comment to let us know who
your favorite scream queen is...

